actually used and consumed

00:05:17.791 --> 00:05:18.290
by users.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.900
So a very high-level overview.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.210
The point here is that
this session, we'll

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:27.200
talk about the full life cycle,
and GCP data platform is built

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.980
to address the full lifecycle.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.840
So we'll talk about
individual services

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.300
and their capabilities,
but in the end,

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.610
maybe the most important
thing is actually not

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:39.120
what each service does.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.550
Its what they have in common.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:45.110
It's the key principles that
are at the foundation of Google

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:50.060
Cloud and that shine through
all of the services, so one

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.460
of them being integrated.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.710
You know, the last thing
we want is data silos.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:57.070
And a lot of customers--
especially those who move from

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.167
on-prem systems--

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.750
they're moving from
a very siloed view

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.350
of the world, where some data
is in the data warehouse.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:04.940
Some data is in
the Hadoop cluster.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.040
Some data is somewhere else.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.060
And where the data is limits
what you can do with it.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:15.890
And so this we a long time
ago rejected internally.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.500
And when the time came for
us to build Google Cloud,

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:23.060
we've brought that philosophy of
separating processing from data

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.700
and having data in
all storage system

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.780
accessible from
all pricing system.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.550
And we'll see that in practice.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.460
And it has a drastic effect.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.640
You know, it's simpler.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.710
It's more effective.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.080
But going back to the
collaboration and exploration

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.500
use cases I describe, it
really opens up the door

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.420
to a lot more and much faster
usage and collaboration.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:45.530
Serverless is the other big one.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.270
It's the fact that
moving to Cloud

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:50.450
does not just mean not
dealing with hardware anymore.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.640
That's a very basic
version of Cloud.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.530
Moving to Cloud
really should mean

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:57.890
not having to worry about the
how, about the infrastructure,

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.260
allowing you to focus on
bringing your business

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:03.050
expertise, your
understanding of the data,

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.930
describing what you want
to get done, and that's it,

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:08.990
and having the platform
just make it happen,

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.890
and without you having to
set up machine, or configure

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:15.380
clusters, and decide how
many workers you need,

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.380
things like that.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.130
Serverless takes that
burden away from you,

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.600
and we take care of it.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.850
And then finally, openness.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.940
Everything we do is either
a cloud-native service

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:29.040
that we built from the start
as a multi-tenant serverless

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.570
system or a service where we
took the best of open source

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.160
and brought it to Google.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.240
In the first case, even though
it's something that originated

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:42.110
at Google, we always open source
the tool itself-- the SDK,

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.460
the relevant pieces--

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.790
such that, as you use those
cloud-native services on Google

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.610
Cloud, what you're
using is open source

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.600
tools, standard interfaces, such
that there's never any locking,

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.370
and there is a
rich community that

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.690
builds on top of those tools.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:59.120
And we'll see that in practice
when we talk about some

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.400
of those tools.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.980
So let's now move to the
second part of the session.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.150
And Win is going to set
