01:11:06.792 --> 01:11:08.684
Let's say view, instead.

01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:13.950
And yes.

01:11:13.950 --> 01:11:14.980
And there you go.

01:11:14.980 --> 01:11:16.460
Kelly now has access.

01:11:16.460 --> 01:11:17.500
So there you go.

01:11:17.500 --> 01:11:19.150
I want to pass over
to Reza to show

01:11:19.150 --> 01:11:21.610
one final piece, which is
the Google Spreadsheets

01:11:21.610 --> 01:11:23.490
integration.

01:11:23.490 --> 01:11:26.670
REZA ROKNI: So this was very
recently announced as well.

01:11:26.670 --> 01:11:28.930
So this is Google Sheets.

01:11:28.930 --> 01:11:31.970
And just very quickly,
going to run through here.

01:11:31.970 --> 01:11:34.970
In the sheet, if I go
to the Data column--

01:11:34.970 --> 01:11:36.740
so I'm in Google Sheets now--

01:11:36.740 --> 01:11:39.170
at the bottom, we now
have data connectors.

01:11:39.170 --> 01:11:41.800
And we can choose BigQuery.

01:11:41.800 --> 01:11:44.280
Here, I'll be able
to choose a project.

01:11:44.280 --> 01:11:49.745
So let's go to our
DA Next project.

01:11:49.745 --> 01:11:50.810
Do it right.

01:11:50.810 --> 01:11:53.630
Here we see the
information, the datasets,

01:11:53.630 --> 01:11:56.030
et cetera available to us.

01:11:56.030 --> 01:12:00.650
If I just go back here, I have
created a dataset already.

01:12:00.650 --> 01:12:03.590
If you remember, we were
scanning some products in.

01:12:03.590 --> 01:12:06.680
This happens to be the product
code that was available.

01:12:06.680 --> 01:12:09.560
Here, we have the
sheet which is actually

01:12:09.560 --> 01:12:12.710
going to that table and
existing information.

01:12:12.710 --> 01:12:14.880
If I refresh the
sheet, it's going

01:12:14.880 --> 01:12:19.160
to get the very latest data
that we had, based off the demo.

01:12:19.160 --> 01:12:21.590
So these were the
last items, and plenty

01:12:21.590 --> 01:12:24.470
of chocolate biscuits were
